\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father of men, in whom are one
\par All humankind beneath Thy sun,
\par Stablish our work in Thee begun.
\par Except the house be built of Thee;
\par In vain the builders' toil must be:
\par O strengthen our infirmity!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Man lives not for himself alone,
\par In others' good he finds his own.
\par Life's worth in fellowship is known.
\par We, friends and comrades on life's way,
\par Gather within these walls to pray:
\par Bless Thou our fellowship to- day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Christ, our   elder Brother, who
\par By sering man God's will didst do;
\par Help us  to serve our brethren too,
\par Guide us to seek the things above,
\par The base to shun, the pure approve,
\par To live by Thy free law of love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In all our work, in all our play,
\par Be with us, Lord, our friend, our stay;
\par Lead onward to the perfect day:
\par Then may we know, earth's lesson o'er,
\par With comrades missed or gone before,
\par Heaven's fellowship for evermore.
\par                                    Amen. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

